      "cephalopod_impact": "🐙 Cephalopod impact",
      "cephalopod_ink_contains_active_compoun": "Cephalopod ink contains active compounds being investigated for antibacterial properties — particularly against marine pathogens.",
      "cephalopod_ink_has_been_used_as_a_dye_": "Cephalopod ink has been used as a dye + writing ink since antiquity. The word \"sepia\" (a brown color) comes from the cuttlefish genus Sepia.",
      "cephalopod_ink_has_been_used_in_writin": "Cephalopod ink has been used in writing + art for over 2000 years. The word \"sepia\" (a brown pigment) comes from the cuttlefish genus Sepia.",
      "cephalopod_ink_production_chemistry_fu": "Cephalopod ink: production, chemistry, functions and applications",
      "cephalopod_inspired_aliens_are_now_a_r": "Cephalopod-inspired aliens are now a recurring science-fiction trope. The Heptapods of \"Arrival\" (2016) use radial language reminiscent of octopus distributed intelligence. \"Soma\" video game features deep-sea AI in cephalopod-like bodies. The aliens in \"Annihilation\" reference cephalopod chromatophore biology.",
      "cephalopod_inspired_architecture_has_e": "Cephalopod-inspired architecture has emerged — some buildings + bridges use shell-like load distribution principles derived from nautilus shell biomechanics.",
      "cephalopod_inspired_soft_sculpture": "Cephalopod-inspired soft sculpture",
      "cephalopod_inspired_song_or_poem": "Cephalopod-inspired song or poem",
      "cephalopod_intelligence_camouflage_ink": "Cephalopod intelligence + camouflage + ink + tool use ALL appear to have evolved AFTER the loss of the external shell. Vulnerability drove behavioral complexity.",
      "cephalopod_intelligence_evolved_indepe": "Cephalopod intelligence evolved independently from vertebrate intelligence. What might have driven its evolution?",
      "cephalopod_iridophore_cells_use_stacks": "Cephalopod iridophore cells use stacks of reflectin protein platelets to make BLUE and GREEN — structural color, not pigment color.",
      "cephalopod_jet_noise": "Cephalopod jet noise",
      "cephalopod_lab": "Cephalopod Lab",
